{
  "collections": [
    {
      "description": "Single-tap hopper-game conformance battery for the eval-game-hoppers web app. Drives the game through pagehub-browser and asserts the 5-pillar DOM contract: (1) instant restart, (2) shareable score, (3) content-creator-friendly difficulty, (4) zero install friction, (5) payment via ads — plus gameplay-shape asserts: player species ∈ {kangaroo, rabbit, grasshopper, flea, jerboa} (frog is explicitly forbidden to keep us legally distant from Frogger), data-current-lane increments on tap, deterministic playthrough. Two deterministic navigations: (A) ?seed=hop-test-001&lane-speed=0&lane-density=0&deterministic=1&die-after=6 — lanes do not scroll, no obstacles spawn, each tap advances exactly one lane, and game-over fires after 6 successful taps. The ground-truth simulator (in the platform seed file) is trivial under these params: expected data-current-lane after N taps = N. After die-after fires, the grader exercises pillar 2 (share-url contains score=6 and seed=hop-test-001), pillar 5 (interstitial ad slot + dismiss), then pillar 1 (tap on game-root flips state back to playing, score resets to 0). (B) ?seed=hop-test-001&lane-speed=0&lane-density=0.5&deterministic=1 — same deterministic mode but with density>0 so the world spawns its objects. In deterministic mode objects render at xBase positions (no drift, no collisions), letting the grader assert the gameplay SHAPE without timing flakiness: lane-kind cadence (bank for lane<=0; then repeating grass/road/riverbed for lane=1,2,3 / 4,5,6 / ...), 3 logs per riverbed (uniformly spaced, guarantees every riverbed is hopable), and obstacle-kind attribution. Finally, the grader visits the share URL with a fresh navigate to assert the shared-score-banner renders. Item count is 46, well under the 50-item collection cap.",
      "items": [
        "lifecycle-01-create-session",
        "lifecycle-02-navigate",
        "p4-zero-install-state-playing",
        "p4-no-password-inputs",
        "p4-no-email-inputs",
